    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112232" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρασ-τήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>teller, expounder,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i>of</i> or <i>about</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.5.17
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδῶν φ.</span>
			<i>guide,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				5.4.40
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.243e
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ὀδόντες,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνώμονες</span>
			, the teeth <i>that tell</i> the age, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				421
			</span></i>.</div>
